+
+The assistant tool-call message and each tool result must remain associated, using the tool call ID, so the model can tell which result belongs to which requested action. This matters especially when a response contains multiple tool calls: the harness needs to preserve the call/result relationship before sending the updated history back to the model.
+
+When a result contains an error, that error remains an observation in the conversation. The model can use it to revise its code, call another tool, retry the failed action, or decide to finish rather than treating the failed call as invisible.
 
 The message history is therefore a critical part of the harness.
 
